49	1359	draft	cbse	standard-2	Eng	8	Mathematics	A Letter to God	Learn about naming words	<p>hghhh <span style="font-size: 24px;">bvcfcdfgf <strong>ggggg <em>hhhhhhgghg</em></strong></span></p><h1>Mathematics – Introduction to Fractions</h1><h2>What is a Fraction?</h2><p>A fraction represents a part of a whole. It consists of two parts:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Numerator:</strong> The number above the line, showing how many parts are taken.</p></li><li><p><strong>Denominator:</strong> The number below the line, showing the total number of equal parts.</p></li></ul><p>For example, in the fraction <strong>3/4</strong>:</p><ul><li><p>Numerator = <strong>3</strong></p></li><li><p>Denominator = <strong>4</strong></p></li></ul><p>This means 3 out of 4 equal parts are considered.</p><h2>Types of Fractions</h2><ol><li><p><strong>Proper Fraction:</strong> The numerator is smaller than the denominator.</p><ul><li><p>Example: <strong>2/5</strong></p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Improper Fraction:</strong> The numerator is greater than or equal to the denominator.</p><ul><li><p>Example: <strong>7/4</strong></p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Mixed Fraction:</strong> A combination of a whole number and a proper fraction.</p><ul><li><p>Example: <strong>1 3/4</strong></p></li></ul></li></ol><h2>Basic Operations</h2><h3>Addition</h3><p>When the denominators are the same:</p><ul><li><p><strong>2/8 + 3/8 = 5/8</strong></p></li></ul><h3>Subtraction</h3><ul><li><p><strong>7/10 − 2/10 = 5/10 = 1/2</strong></p></li></ul><h3>Multiplication</h3><p>Multiply the numerators and denominators:</p><ul><li><p><strong>2/3 × 3/5 = 6/15 = 2/5</strong></p></li></ul><h3>Division</h3><p>Multiply by the reciprocal:</p><ul><li><p><strong>3/4 ÷ 2/5 = 3/4 × 5/2 = 15/8 = 1 7/8</strong></p></li></ul><h2>Practice Questions</h2><ol><li><p>Simplify <strong>12/18</strong>.</p></li><li><p>Add <strong>5/9 + 2/9</strong>.</p></li><li><p>Subtract <strong>9/12 − 4/12</strong>.</p></li><li><p>Multiply <strong>4/7 × 7/8</strong>.</p></li><li><p>Divide <strong>5/6 ÷ 1/3</strong>.</p></li></ol><h2>Key Points</h2><ul><li><p>A fraction shows a part of a whole.</p></li><li><p>Always simplify fractions when possible.</p></li><li><p>For addition and subtraction, denominators must be the same.</p></li><li><p>Multiplication and division follow different rules than addition and subtraction.</p></li><li><p>Fractions are widely used in daily life, such as measuring ingredients, calculating discounts, and dividing objects into equal parts.</p></li></ul><p></p>	<h1>Demo Content</h1><p>This is a sample paragraph created for testing purposes. It contains enough text to verify layouts, typography, spacing, and other UI elements. The content is generic and does not represent any real information.</p><p>Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. Sed do eiusmod tempor incididunt ut labore et dolore magna aliqua. Ut enim ad minim veniam, quis nostrud exercitation ullamco laboris nisi ut aliquip ex ea commodo consequat.</p><h2>Features</h2><ul><li><p>Easy to read</p></li><li><p>Suitable for testing</p></li><li><p>Placeholder text for development</p></li><li><p>Works well in cards, tables, and forms</p></li></ul><p>Thank you for using this demo content. You can replace this text with actual content whenever needed.</p>	Happy First Teacher	\N	\N	2026-07-14 06:49:49.822011	\N	2026-07-14 06:49:49.822016	\N	5	Academic	\N	\N	\N	\N
